# Proposed by the executor of F68 (2026-10-15), from what two adversarial readers played; the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: with nothing left over, what floats lies over the docked windows, and is still its person's.
# Reference: F68.
quiet
open Safari
open Terminal
open Notes
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
# A click on the floating window, and ⌃⌥↓ at once: the pointer is on Notes, so the step goes to the Desktop, not to what is docked under it.
cursor 500 400
focus 103
press in
expect camera desktop
expect visible 103
show-all
# Undo while the view on record is on a window that is in the Dock: everything shows, and so does what floats.
zoom 102
float 102
minimize 102
undo
expect visible 103
restore 102
show-all
float-all
# ⌃⌥F on a framed window among three: the other two stay in view.
arrange
zoom 101
float 101
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
float-all
close 103

# What the others lent for the keyboard's sake is not forgotten when the lender leaves: the gap is where it was.
close 101
close 102
open Safari 700x500 min 574x240
open Mail 800x500 min 760x400
open Notes 749x420 min 709x300
focus 104
dock left
focus 105
dock right
expect size 104 644x851
expect size 105 760x851
focus 106
dock right
focus 105
home
close 106
expect size 104 644x851
expect size 105 760x851
close 104
close 105

# The setting switched on over an arrangement made without the column: what `layout` prints is still what is there, and `balance` brings the column.
open A
open B
dock 107 left
dock 108 right
set desktopColumn true
layout --ids
expect replied 107 | Desktop:0 | 108
balance
expect size 107 464x851
expect size 108 464x851
